- @page_title = t('settings')

/! Report a problem (SettingsController#report). The page sends nothing itself: report.js opens a
/! new issue in the browser, the email app, or saves or copies the report.
.kai-report data-issues-url=ProblemReport::ISSUES_URL data-email=ProblemReport::EMAIL data-version=@version data-storage=@storage
  p.mb-2
    = link_to '← Help', settings_help_path
  h2.kai-report-title Report a problem
  p.kai-report-intro
    | Nothing leaves this server until you send it, and you see every word first. Amahi-kai sends
      nothing itself: GitHub or your email app does, from this computer.

  .alert.kai-report-status#report-status role="status" hidden=true

  .card.mb-4
    .card-header.bg-dark.text-white
      h5.mb-0 What went wrong
    .card-body
      .mb-3
        label.form-label for="report-what"
          | What happened
          span.text-muted.ms-1 (needed)
        textarea.form-control#report-what rows="4" required=true aria-describedby="report-what-problem" = @what_happened
        .invalid-feedback#report-what-problem Say what happened, in a few words.
      .mb-3
        label.form-label for="report-expected" What you expected
        textarea.form-control#report-expected rows="2" placeholder="What should have happened instead"
      div
        label.form-label for="report-steps" How to make it happen again
        textarea.form-control#report-steps rows="3" placeholder=("1. Open Apps\n2. Install Transmission\n3. …")

  .card.mb-4
    .card-header.bg-dark.text-white.d-flex.flex-wrap.justify-content-between.align-items-center.gap-2
      h5.mb-0 System details
      .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-2
        span#report-scrub-label Hide names and addresses
        button.kai-switch#report-scrub type="button" role="switch" aria-checked="true" aria-labelledby="report-scrub-label"
          span.kai-switch-knob aria-hidden="true"
    .card-body
      p.small.text-muted#report-scrub-note
        | Addresses, and the names of this server, its users, devices, pools, shares, folders and files, are
          replaced like &lt;share-1&gt;; the same name gets the same stand-in everywhere, so the report still
          makes sense. You can change any of it before you send it.
      label.visually-hidden for="report-details" System details to send
      textarea.form-control.kai-report-details#report-details rows="18" spellcheck="false" = @details
      textarea#report-details-as-is hidden=true aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" = @details_as_is

  .card
    .card-header.bg-dark.text-white
      h5.mb-0 Send it
    .card-body
      .kai-report-ways
        .kai-report-way.kai-report-way-main
          button.btn.btn-primary#report-github type="button" Open on GitHub
          p.small.mb-0 A new issue, filled in, in your browser. You look it over there and submit it. Needs a GitHub account.
        .kai-report-way
          button.btn.btn-outline-light#report-email type="button" Send by email
          p.small.mb-0
            | Opens your email app, addressed to #{ProblemReport::EMAIL}. No GitHub account needed.
        .kai-report-way
          button.btn.btn-outline-light#report-download type="button" Download report
          p.small.mb-0 The whole report as a text file, to attach to an issue or an email.
        .kai-report-way
          button.btn.btn-outline-light#report-copy type="button" Copy
          p.small.mb-0 The whole report, to paste wherever you like.
      p.small.text-muted.mt-3.mb-0
        | A security problem? Don't post it publicly:
        =< link_to 'report a vulnerability privately', 'https://github.com/CatDogBark/Amahi-kai/security/advisories/new', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener'
        | .
